      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Matteo, That is an out-of-date video where a beta release of Fedora 3.0 was used.  I've updated the title to that effect, and have pointed to the latest installation information in the description.</p>\n\n<p>Which version of Fedora are you trying to install?  The procedure is different now.  I would recommend installing the latest version (3.3) using these instructions:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://www.fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/FCR30/Installation+and+Configuration+Guide\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/FCR30/Installation+and+Configuration+Guide</a></p>\n\n<p>This latest version should work fine in your environment, with Java 1.6.  If you continue to have problems, you might also find hints as to what is wrong in the $FEDORA_HOME/server/logs/fedora.log file and/or the tomcat/logs/catalina.out file.</p>\n\n<p>Also, we have a mailing list for technical questions which you may want to sign up for.  Details are here:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"http://www.fedora-commons.org/community/userlist\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.fedora-commons.org/community/userlist</a></p>",
     "created": "11/May/10 12:26 PM",
     "id": "11365",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10495/comment/11365",
